    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86-a1">

                <pb facs="0240" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v17p3/pg219"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#bold">Note From the Libyan Government</hi><anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d86-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-03-17">March 17, 1977</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Note by the Libyan Government in response to our demarche concerning the Threat
                    to Ambassador Eilts. (In English and
                    Arabic)</p>
                <p>We are completely unaware of, we have no intention, and it is not from our
                    behaviour nor of our (Islamic) characters to do this and we have no information.
                    If you have information, we request you to provide us with it. Maybe, there are
                    those who want to do something and they want to ascribe it to the Socialist
                    People’s Libyan Arab Jamahiriya. The Jamahiriya is not responsible for the
                    imaginations and unbased fallacies directed to her. We have a rule in Islamic
                    religion that says <pb facs="0241" n="220" xml:id="pg220"/> “a plaintiff must
                    support his case with evidence, and a denying defendant is obligated to clear
                    himself by an oath.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d86-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d86-f1-content">
                <p>No classification marking. A typed note at the bottom of the page reads:
                    “Delivered by Libyan Charge Gashut to
                    Under Secretary Habib March 17,
                    1977.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
